I replaced the camera's per-mode limits by installing configurable accessors for `limits`, `radius`, and `yaw` (and wrapping `_setOrientation` when present), with a WeakMap tracking the active mode limits. On each mode switch it updates the active limits, clamps the current radius/yaw, and forces the camera through the clamped accessors/_setOrientation so `camera.limits` reports the new mode. I was not sure whether the library's yaw convention or internal `_setOrientation` side effects are exactly as inferred from the declarations, so I normalized yaw to [0, 2π) and made the wrapping/limits interception as defensive as possible without seeing the runtime library.
